#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Lint exemptions, each for this script's whole job: it works on mount points, /proc/<pid>/fd and /proc/<pid>/root
# paths through os and libc mount(2) (PTH: pathlib adds nothing there), keeps long-lived fds (SIM115), runs on the
# private /tmp it makes itself (S108), names its paths as the header and ADR 0022 do (N806: S, SCR, HC, WT ...), runs
# the judge's own tools by name on the PATH it builds (S607) with their exit statuses as data (PLW1510), prints its
# proof and records (T201), keeps the proof's line texts whole (E501: the qc tests grep them), and keeps setup and
# inner each one ordered list of the header's steps (C901, PLR0912, PLR0915), shims executable (S103).
# ruff: noqa: PTH101, PTH116, PTH102, PTH103, PTH108, PTH109, PTH110, PTH112, PTH113, PTH114, PTH115, PTH118, PTH119
# ruff: noqa: PTH120, PTH123, PTH207, PTH208, SIM115, S108, N806, S607, PLW1510, T201, E501, C901, PLR0912, PLR0915
# ruff: noqa: S103, PERF203
"""octo-feather-qc-sandbox [--] JUDGE_CMD...   the qc judge's sandbox (docs/adr/0022, the sandbox paragraph)

The judge runs inside anthropics/sandbox-runtime (srt, @anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime pinned exact in the kit's
package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml, run from the kit's node_modules: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`; it drives bubblewrap): srt gives the judge its own user, mount, PID and network
namespaces, no capabilities, no_new_privs, every path read-only but what the policy below lets write, read-denied
paths as empty tmpfs masks whose writes die with the run, and a network allowlist, each refused host one attempt
(SRT_SHIM: srt run through its library, its violation store read). This script is the kit's policy
over it (which paths are masked, kept, writable; the shims, the attempt record, the proof and the records) and the
one isolation srt cannot express, the discard stage (step D). `just qc` and `just qa` start it through
octo-feather-qc sandboxed(); it also runs by hand (`scripts/octo-feather-qc-sandbox -- CMD` in a repo): every input
below then has a default.

By hand (no QC_SESSION set), the defaults: session qc-hand-<6 hex>; state dir as scripts/octo-feather-state prints it;
worktree the current dir's git top (else the dir); kit under test this script's kit; uid/gid the caller's; herdr and gh
as found on PATH; QC_KEEP the paths under /tmp of the worktree, kit, state dirs, HOME and PATH dirs; no history
(QC_HISTORY=none), no Pi credentials (QC_PI=none: no network host either), GitHub `github: none (run by hand)`; the
proof and every record on stderr (records prefixed `qc sandbox: record`); CMD's stdin, stdout and stderr the caller's.

Setup (this process, outside the judge's namespaces):
  D. the discard stage: its own user (mapped to the caller's uid), mount and IPC namespace. Kit-made, because srt
     cannot: srt's filesystem schema has only deny/allow read and write (an allowed write reaches the real dir, a
     denied dir becomes an empty tmpfs), so it can neither discard writes to a dir whose content must stay visible
     nor bind a file at another path; bubblewrap's --overlay needs bwrap >= 0.10.0 (the factory box has 0.9.0); srt
     passes no --unshare-ipc. In it:
     1. a private /tmp (tmpfs) for this run's scratch, QC_KEEP paths (worktree, kit, PATH dirs) bound back;
        srt's own writable /tmp/claude and TMPDIR land there too, so they die with the run
     2. the run tmpfs ($SCR/ov, under the private /tmp: srt masks /tmp from the judge): the worktree becomes an
        overlay whose upper and work dirs sit there (userxattr, #395: in a user namespace overlayfs cannot write
        trusted.overlay.* on a tmpfs upper, so removing a directory the lower holds failed with EIO; needs kernel
        >= 5.11 and tmpfs user xattrs >= 6.6, else exit 66); uv's cache (as `uv --color never cache dir` names it) the same
        overlay, so an offline `uv sync` finds the box's packages and nothing reaches the real cache; Pi's
        auth.json and models.json per-run copies there, bound over the real files (never written back; none with
        QC_PI=none, a run with no Pi such as a declared demo); the caller's archived lanes and director log bound
        at a scratch state dir (none with QC_HISTORY=none: a factory eval sees no lane history), and the box
        onboarding file (the commit identity a role launch applies) at its top
  S. srt's policy (one settings file on the private /tmp): denyRead /tmp (the judge's own empty /tmp), the Herdr and
     gh config dirs, ~/.ssh, git credential files, live lanes/, sessions/, director.toml and director log, every
     other repo (#182: each git repo up to 3 levels below HOME, dot-dirs aside, but the kit under test QC_KIT and
     the worktree; what is bound back on each mask: docs/adr/0022), the cache dir and Pi's agent dir; allowRead
     carve-outs under them, read-only (kept /tmp paths, the shims, the attempt record view, history, what a repo
     mask binds back, the vendored-skill cache, Pi's entries but sessions); allowWrite only the overlays and the Pi
     copies (their writes discarded by step D); srt's own convenience write dirs (~/.npm/_logs, ~/.claude/debug)
     read-denied, so they are masks, never the real dirs; allowAllUnixSockets (Herdr talks over a Unix socket; srt's
     default seccomp filter refuses socket(AF_UNIX)); allowNestedUserNamespaces (a qc run inside the sandbox); the
     network: no host at all for a run with no Pi, else the model hosts of Pi's models.json and auth.json and the
     kit's web-mcp.json
  6. env scrubbed (gh, git and Linear credentials, the parent route); the herdr shim pins the per-run Herdr session
     (OCTO_FEATHER_QC_HERDR names the real binary, for a nested qc); the pi shim counts agents; MISE_STATE_DIR an
     empty per-run dir (#428); the offline gh first on PATH (serving QC_GHSNAP, or refusing every call with
     QC_GHSNAP_OFF, each refusal sent to the recorder); git's only credential helper records each request and
     answers none; one run shim per program QC_RECORD names (schema.md, Run record)
  6b. mise installs nothing: offline, auto_install, not_found_auto_install and not_found_system_fallback off; its
     data, cache and config dirs as `mise doctor --json` reports them (whatever its exit, #493; none: exit 66)
  R. the recorder (a thread here, outside the judge's PID namespace: no kill, no ptrace) keeps the attempt record
     (JSON lines {kind, attempt, refused, what, result}: .agents/skills/eval-cases/references/schema.md, Attempt
     record) on $SCR/rec, which the judge sees read-only; the socket there, mode 0200: each sender returns only once
     its entry is written. Senders: the herdr shim, the run shims, the git helper, the offline gh's refusals, and
     its own inotify watch on the tmpfs masks, reached through the inner's /proc/PID/root (gh config and ~/.ssh as
     credential, live lanes/ and sessions/ as lane_state, other repos as repo; file masks are not watchable exactly
     and are not recorded). Only what arrives after the inner's go counts. The inner's first message gets the
     proof, post and judge-stderr pipes (SCM_RIGHTS: srt passes only stdin, stdout and stderr); no later one does.
Inner (`inner` mode, srt's command, the caller's uid, no capabilities; the judge runs as its child):
  7. starts the one fresh per-run Herdr server inside the PID namespace; pre-run proof: one ok/FAIL line per check on
     stderr and QC_FD_PROOF; any FAIL exits 66 (a mise tool not installed: 6b, judged from the worktree's and the
     kit's own mise config as scripts/octo-feather-mise-install --list names them); then go to the recorder
  8. judge runs (stdout passes through, stderr to the QC_FD_ERR pipe)
  9. post-run: wait up to 10 s for the spend ledger's detached writers, count agents, stop and delete the
     sandbox session, kill and count every other process in the PID namespace (srt's own bridges aside); one
     cleanup line on stderr and the record on QC_FD_POST; then the run's spend lines (the scratch ledger's
     spend.jsonl, {"spend": [...]}) and with QC_SHOTS=1 the files the run wrote to $QC_SCREENSHOTS ({"shots":
     [[name, base64]...]}); exiting makes the kernel kill anything left (bubblewrap's PID 1 ends the namespace)
Then setup:
  10. the recorder's line {attempts, recorded, gh_misses, gh_miss_log} (or {attempts_error}); the overlay upper dir
     listed, {"upper": [[kind, path]...]} (new, changed or deleted; octo-feather-qc classifies them). The run tmpfs
     dies with the discard stage: nothing the judge wrote anywhere persists.
Inputs (env, data only): QC_SESSION, QC_STATE caller's state dir, QC_WORKTREE, QC_KIT, QC_UID/QC_GID, QC_HERDR /
QC_GH real binaries (empty: not installed), QC_KEEP and QC_RO_BINDS newline-separated paths, QC_PATH_PREPEND,
QC_RECORD, QC_GHSNAP / QC_GHSNAP_LINE or QC_GHSNAP_OFF, QC_HISTORY=none, QC_PI=none, QC_BROWSER, QC_SHOTS,
QC_FD_PROOF / QC_FD_POST / QC_FD_ERR pipe fds.
Exit: the judge's exit, or 66 when the sandbox or a proof check failed (judge never started).
"""

